hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16180","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Wail, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Zaynab wife of Abdullah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to women: Give charity, even of your jewelry. She said: And Abdullah was light of means. So she said to him: Does it suffice me to put my charity in thee and in sons of my brother, or sons of a brother of mine, orphans? So Abdullah said: Ask about that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and on his door was a woman of the Ansar called Zaynab asking about what I ask about. So Bilal came out to us, and we said: Go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him about that, and do not inform who we are. So he went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Who are they? He said: Zaynab. He said: Which of the Zaynabs? He said: Zaynab wife of Abdullah, and Zaynab the Ansariyyah. So he said: Yes, for them are two rewards: the reward of kinship and the reward of charity."
"16181","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Mansur, from Amr ibn al-Harith ibn al-Mustaliq, from Zaynab wife of Abdullah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us with charity and said: Give charity, O company of women. And he mentioned the hadith."
"16182","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Amr ibn al-Harith ibn al-Mustaliq, from Zaynab, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give charity, O company of women. And he mentioned it."
